### VictoriaMetrics operator

With `operator.enabled: true` the chart renders a [VLAgent](https://docs.victoriametrics.com/operator/resources/vlagent/) resource
instead of its own StatefulSet, Service, ServiceAccount and VPA,
and the [VictoriaMetrics operator](https://docs.victoriametrics.com/operator/) manages the workload.
The operator must already be installed in the cluster. Operator mode always uses operator-style names, regardless of `useLegacyNaming`.

The VLAgent is named after the release (or `fullnameOverride`), so the operator creates `vlagent-<release>` objects.
Instead of rendering its own scrape object, the chart lets the operator create the VMServiceScrape when `serviceMonitor.enabled` is enabled, and disables it otherwise.

The spec is built from chart values: image, replicas, resources, scheduling, env, extra args, volumes, containers,
pod metadata, security context, HTTP listen port, Service settings, service account and license. In addition:

- `networkPolicy` ingress and egress rules become the resource `networkPolicy`, and the operator creates the NetworkPolicy. Its labels and annotations can't be set;
- `remoteWrite` entries become VLAgent `remoteWrite` the way the chart renders them: a URL without a path gets `/insert/native`, TLS flags become `tlsConfig` and `headers` maps become header lists. Inline credentials and settings the VLAgent doesn't support can't be converted;
- `maxDiskUsagePerURL` becomes `remoteWriteSettings.maxDiskUsagePerURL`;
- `syslog` listeners become `syslogSpec`;
- `persistentVolume` becomes the `storage` claim template with the chart's claim name, so existing claims are kept, and `existingClaim` is mounted as the queue volume;
- `verticalPodAutoscaler` becomes `vpa`. `horizontalPodAutoscaler` isn't supported by the VLAgent and fails the rendering.

Fields that have no chart value, or need a different value, go to `operator.spec`, which is deep-merged over the generated spec:

```yaml
operator:
  enabled: true
  spec:
    logLevel: WARN
```

Rendering fails for settings that have no operator equivalent, with a message pointing to `operator.spec`.
Probes keep the operator defaults. Switching a release to `operator.enabled: true` recreates its pods.

